 for \"common cover transitive\" actions. We give some infinite families of common cover transitive actions and show that the common cover transitive actions are closed under direct and semidirect products.\n\n\nContent available from Order\n\nThis content is subject to copyright. Terms and conditions apply.\n\nOrder (2017) 34:441–463\n\nDOI 10.1007/s11083-016-9408-x\n\nPeckness of Edge Posets\n\nDavid Hemminger 1·Aaron Landesman 2·Zijian Yao 3\n\nReceived: 18 March 2015 / Accepted: 1 September 2016 / Published online: 6 October 2016\n\n© Springer Science+Business Media Dordrecht 2016\n\nAbstract For any graded poset P, we define a new graded poset, E(P ), whose elements are\n\nthe edges in the Hasse diagram of P. For any group G acting on the boolean algebra B n in a\n\nrank-preserving fashion we conjecture that E(B n/G) is Peck. We prove that the conjecture\n\nholds for “common cover transitive” actions. We give some infinite families of common\n\ncover transitive actions and show that the common cover transitive actions are closed under\n\ndirect and semidirect products.\n\nKeywords Boolean algebra ·Edges ·Group actions ·Peck posets ·Quotient posets ·\n\nUnimodality\n\n1 Introduction\n\nLet P be a finite graded poset of rank n. In this paper we study the structure of the edges in\n\nthe Hasse diagram of P. To this end, we define an endofunctor E on the category of finite\n\ngraded posets with rank-preserving morphisms.\n\nDavid Hemminger\n\ndhemminger@math.ucla.edu\n\nAaron Landesman\n\naaronlandesman@gmail.com\n\nZijian Yao\n\nzijian.yao.math@gmail.com\n\n1 Duke University, 6300 Lakeland Dr., Raleigh, NC 27612, USA\n\n2 Harvard University, 323 Eliot Mail Center, Cambridge, MA 02138, USA\n\n3 Brown University, 7285 Brown University, Providence, RI 02912, USA--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPeckness of Edge Posets - arXiv Combinatorics (https://arxiv.symmetricfunctions.com/paper/1501.04540v2)\nciteturn0search1 [